{"t":"2026-07-30T08:07:03Z","eid":"83fd8196b4a4f224","ag":"ag-bee2","ev":"create","id":"B-01KYS1028RE8NTN07F6HSGBRPH","k":"bug","ti":"capGist doc comment is attached to the wrong symbol, its ordering contract is unpinned, and its comment overstates the coverage","dir":"internal/lifecycle"}
{"t":"2026-07-30T08:07:24Z","eid":"4594e8f570fda86e","ag":"ag-67ff","ev":"move","id":"B-01KYS1028RE8NTN07F6HSGBRPH","dir":"internal/lifecycle","fr":"draft","to":"active","note":"three defects in text and test coverage of the change that just shipped, all from a verdict that arrived after the record archived"}
{"t":"2026-07-30T08:12:26Z","eid":"488941b519580aaa","ag":"ag-0df7","ev":"move","id":"B-01KYS1028RE8NTN07F6HSGBRPH","dir":"internal/lifecycle","fr":"active","to":"done","note":"All three fixed. The var moved above capGist doc comment with a blank line between them, so go doc now attributes each paragraph to its own symbol - verified by reading go doc -u output for both, not by assuming the blank line was enough. The CRLF-first ordering is pinned by TestCapGistCollapsesLineEndings using exact string equality, because a contains-no-newline assertion passes for BOTH orderings and would not have caught it; reordering the replacer to match LF first now fails with capGist of a-CRLF-b returning two spaces instead of one, confirmed by mutation. The overstated comment is narrowed to name CommonMark as the contract the bullet is rendered under, states which separators are deliberately not touched - U+2028, U+2029, U+0085, VT, FF - and says why widening the set needs a measurement; the same test pins that boundary from the other side, asserting those five survive, so a future widening fails a test rather than happening silently. Suite green. Worth recording plainly: defect 2 was this repository committing the exact error it had just written a fix for - a behavioral guarantee living only in prose - one function away from the fix. That it took an independent verifier mutating the code to find it, while the whole suite stayed green, is the argument for the mutation check rather than for more comments."}
